## Result (2026-08-19)

[Asset: Effect Schema Contracts for Observational Memory](./asset-effect-schema-observational-contracts.svx) records the v3.19.17 joelclaw contract, the v4 content-grill reference, official Effect source receipts, schema-v1 gaps, persistence and parse-error rules, and the recommendation to put the semantic core in a new standalone repository. `joelclaw` remains the accepted-Run integration/composition root, and `joelclaw-observer` remains the host adapter. The command and source receipt report is `/tmp/observational-memory-effect-schema-research.md`. No implementation source or brief was changed.

Proposed decision-ledger entry: use versioned Effect Schemas for observations, reflections, evidence, projector state, migrations, persistence, and search; keep the semantic core in a new standalone repo shaped like content-grill, with joelclaw and joelclaw-observer as adapters.
